# Source for s1-sbz1-tube.bk2 (InputLogAuthorTool --script). Scrap Brain Act 1 from its level
# start: the recorded complete run with native lag rows not replayed, and one authored change:
# Down for 8 frames as Sonic lands at the tube mouth, so he rolls into the tube and stays in a
# ball through it (Sonic_Roll; Scrap Brain has no roll-tunnel chunks, LoopChunkNums in
# _inc/LevelSizeLoad & BgScrollSpeed.asm:222-228, so the recording ran upright there).
# Derived with GameplayInputBranchTool from s1-complete-run.bk2 (not edited by hand):
#   GameplayInputBranchTool --skip-rows <the 72 rows below> --input-start 163354 --resume 420
#     <s1 ROM> s1 sbz 1 320 sonic none src/test/resources/traces/s1/_movies/s1-complete-run.bk2
#     4918 <out> '8 D'
# Skipped rows:
#     165282, 165568, 166099, 166177, 166291, 166322, 166372, 166389, 166408, 166519, 166647,
#     166649, 166727, 166845, 166887, 166889, 166894, 166901, 166909, 166914, 166918, 166923,
#     166926, 166928, 167055, 167081, 167096, 167101, 167107, 167252, 167300, 167425, 167458,
#     167488, 167492, 167525, 167558, 167591, 167624, 167728, 167733, 167760, 167763, 167774,
#     167779, 167784, 167786, 167789, 167792, 167797, 167801, 167803, 167806, 167808, 167811,
#     167815, 167818, 167823, 167830, 167836, 167838, 167840, 167852, 167901, 168219, 168291,
#     168335, 168417, 168431, 168456, 168785, 168842
# --skip-rows lists the movie rows 163354 + r for every sbz1_completerun row r < 5500 where
# gameplay_frame_counter repeats (a native lag frame: VBlank_Lag, sonic.asm:711-712, does not
# reach ReadJoypads, so the pad was not polled there). With them dropped, the replay matches the
# trace's positions up to the Down press (all 5,336 frames without it), with or without the
# Sonic 2 donor.
